A Rust port of Plasmo Voice by Plasmo (Apehum, KPidS and contributors),
https://github.com/plasmoapp/plasmo-voice (branch main, commit 198ad94,
version 2.2.0), whose code and assets are under the GNU Lesser General Public
License version 3 (LICENSE). This port is under the same licence.

From Plasmo Voice, unchanged:
- the icons in mixins/plasmovoice/data/ (client/src/main/resources/assets/
  plasmovoice/textures/icons/, its tabs/ as tab_*.png, and icon.png);
- the English texts (client lang/en_us.json), in mixins/plasmovoice/lang.rs;
- the server's English texts (server/common languages/en_us.toml), in
  mixins/plasmovoice/engine/src/lang/en_us.toml;
- the server config's comments and layout (VoiceServerConfig, written by
  plo-config), in mixins/plasmovoice/engine/src/server_config.rs, and a
  config.toml PlasmoVoice-Paper 2.2.0-beta.3 wrote, as a test fixture in
  mixins/plasmovoice/engine/src/testdata/plasmo-config.toml.

The Russian texts are Plasmo Voice's own Crowdin translations
(https://github.com/plasmoapp/plasmo-voice-crowdin, branch pv: ru_RU/client.json
and the Proximity names of each language's server.toml; ru_RU/server.toml
whole, in mixins/plasmovoice/engine/src/lang/ru_ru.toml), translations of the
LGPL-3.0 strings above.

Plasmo Voice's Mod Menu screen is built with Cloth Config by shedaniel
(https://github.com/shedaniel/cloth-config, LGPL-3.0): its look is rewritten
in Rust (mixins/plasmovoice/cloth.rs), its arrows and buttons in
mixins/plasmovoice/cloth_sprites.rs are parts of Cloth Config's texture.

Noise suppression is RNNoise as Plasmo Voice runs it (its rnnoise-jni-rust wraps
nnnoiseless 0.5.2): nnnoiseless by Joe Neeman (https://github.com/jneem/nnnoiseless,
tag v0.5.2, BSD-3-Clause), a Rust port of RNNoise by Jean-Marc Valin
(Xiph.Org Foundation, Mozilla), with RNNoise's trained model (weights.rnn),
copied into mixins/plasmovoice/engine/src/rnnoise/ (the model as Rust,
weights.rs), its FFT rewritten after Mark Borgerding's KISS FFT. Their licence
